{"id": "jdi-2026-07-13-008", "date": "2026-07-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 29, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": ["jdi", "lg_elec", "lg_display"], "customers": ["lg_elec"], "suppliers": ["lg_display"]}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.9, "reasons": ["多公司提及", "供應鏈上下游同時提及"]}, "title": "LG Display said to accelerate its plans to convert some of its 8-Gen WOLED fab in Paju to eLEAP AMOLED production", "content": "<p>Last year, we <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/lg-display-looking-adopting-jdis-eleap-maskless-deposition-technology-its-oled\">reported</a> that LG Display is looking into adopting <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/japan-display\">Japan Display</a>'s eLEAP technology at its OLED TV production lines in Paju, perhaps seeking to produce RGB AMOLED displays for IT applications at these fabs that are currently under utilized. In April 2026, we <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/lg-display-advanc", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/lg-display-said-accelerate-its-plans-convert-some-its-8-gen-woled-fab-paju", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "lg_elec-2026-07-13-009", "date": "2026-07-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 29, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": ["lg_elec", "boe"], "customers": ["lg_elec"], "suppliers": ["boe"]}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.9, "reasons": ["多公司提及", "供應鏈上下游同時提及"]}, "title": "Reports suggest BOE struggles to get approval for its Nanjing WOLED production line project", "content": "<p>In May 2026 we <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/will-boe-convert-its-b18-85-gen-lcd-fab-nanjing-woled-production\">reported</a> that BOE is looking to upgrade its pilot WOLED (WRGB) production capabilities. According to the company's plan back then, it would convert some of its B18 8.5-Gen LCD fab in Nanjing to WOLED production.</p><img src=\"https://www.oled-info.com/sites/default/files/oled_company_profile/oled_company_profileLG-Ultragear-45GR95QE-img_assist-400x225.jpg\" alt=\"LG Ultragear 4", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/reports-suggest-boe-struggles-get-approval-its-nanjing-woled-production-line", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "csot-2026-07-13-010", "date": "2026-07-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 29, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": ["csot", "tcl"], "customers": ["tcl"], "suppliers": ["csot"]}, "topics": ["panel_price", "oled_penetration", "it_panel_demand"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.9, "reasons": ["多公司提及", "供應鏈上下游同時提及"]}, "title": "TCL CSOT starts producing 27\" 4K inkjet printed OLED monitor panels at its 5.5-Gen line in Wuhan", "content": "<p>In March we <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/tcl-csot-start-producing-consumer-27-4k-inkjet-printed-oled-panels-july-2026\">reported</a> that TCL CSOT's first consumer-grade inkjet printed OLED display has completed functional verification, and the company is planning to mass produce these panels in July 2026. There are now reports that the company is indeed starting production of this panel.</p><p><img src=\"https://www.oled-info.com/sites/default/files/inline-images/TCL-CSOT-27-inch-printed", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/tcl-csot-starts-producing-27-4k-inkjet-printed-oled-monitor-panels-its-55-gen", "type": "rss"}]}
